-- title:
--   Primes over a supersingular point: trichotomy, and one end per component
-- statement:
--   **Data and standing hypotheses.** Let $q\ge 5$ and $\ell\ge 3$ be primes with $\ell\neq q$, and let $M'$ be a nonzero natural number with $q\nmid M'$ (`hqM'`) and $\ell\nmid M'$ (`hℓM'`). Let $L$ be a field of characteristic $0$, let $\xi\in L$ be a primitive $q\ell$-th root of unity (`hξ`), and let `hι` be the hypothesis that some ring homomorphism $\iota:L\to\mathbb C$ sends $\xi$ to $\exp(2\pi i/(q\ell))$. Let $K$ be an intermediate field of $L\subseteq \operatorname{LaurentSeries} L$ which (`hK`) equals [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange L`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103) applied to [`ModularCurve.xHFunctionField ((q*ℓ)^2*M') (ModularCurve.FullLevel.levelH (q*ℓ) M')`](def/ModularCurve_XH.html#L79): that is, $K$ is the $L$-subfield of $L((t))$ generated by the coefficientwise image of the $q$-expansion function field of $X_H$ of level $(q\ell)^2M'$, with $H$ the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb Z/(q\ell)^2M')^\times\to(\mathbb Z/q\ell)^\times$.
--
--   Let $A$ be a discrete valuation ring and domain, an $A$-algebra structure on $L$ making $L$ the fraction field of $A$, with $A$ henselian local and $\operatorname{ResidueField} A$ algebraically closed; assume $q\in\mathfrak m_A$ (`hAq`) and that $\xi$ lies in the image of $A$ (`hξA`); $K$ is an $A$-algebra compatibly with $A\to L\to K$. Let $j\in K$ be nonzero whose image in $L((t))$ is the coefficientwise image of the $q$-expansion [`ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L157) of the modular $j$-invariant (`hj`). Let $\varpi$ generate $\mathfrak m_A$ (`hϖ`), and let $\varpi_t\in A$ satisfy $\varpi_t^{\,q^2-1}=q\cdot u$ with $u$ a unit (`hϖt`).
--
--   Write $C:=$ `chartAlgFin A K j`, the $A$-subalgebra of $K$ of elements integral over $A[j]$, and let $\mathfrak X:=$ [`AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel A K j`](def/AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel.html#L236), the pushout of the two affine charts $\operatorname{Spec} C$ and $\operatorname{Spec}$ `chartAlgInf A K j` along the middle chart, with structure morphism `toBase` to $\operatorname{Spec} A$. Let $y\subset C$ be a maximal ideal (`hy`) containing the image of $\varpi$ (`hϖy`) and supersingular in the sense of `hss`: for every algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $q$ and every ring homomorphism $\varphi:C\to\Omega$ with kernel $y$, the element $\varphi(j)$ lies in [`ModularCurve.ssJSet q Ω`](def/ModularCurve_SupersingularModuli.html#L7), the set of those $j_0\in\Omega$ such that every elliptic curve over $\Omega$ with $j$-invariant $j_0$ has trivial $q$-torsion.
--
--   **The chart hypothesis `hArig`.** This hypothesis asserts, for every point $z$ of $\mathfrak X$, every element $\varpi_z$ of the stalk at $z$ which is the germ of the global section obtained from $\varpi$ along `toBase` (`hϖz`) and lies in the maximal ideal of that stalk (`hz`), and every point $y'$ of `XFin` $=\operatorname{Spec} C$ with `ιFin`$(y')=z$ (`hy'`) whose ideal is supersingular in the above sense (`hss'`), the existence of a complete discrete valuation domain — the bound variable named `W` in `hArig`, written $W_0$ here to avoid collision with the valuation subring `W` introduced below — together with $\sigma:A\to W_0$ with $\mathfrak m_{W_0}=(\sigma\varpi)$, power series $f,u,v\in W_0[[X_0,X_1]]$ with $u,v$ units and $f\equiv X_0X_1^q-X_0^qX_1$ modulo $(X_0,X_1)^{q+2}$ (the Drinfeld form [`DrinfeldCurve.LocalChart.drinfeldForm`](def/DrinfeldCurve_LocalChart.html#L18)), and a ring isomorphism $e$ from the adic completion of the stalk at $z$ onto $S:=W_0[[X_0,X_1]]/\bigl(\sigma(\varpi_t^{\,q+1})v-fu\bigr)$, subject to seven clauses, summarised here: (i) $e$ carries the germ of each $a\in A$ to the constant $\sigma(a)$; (ii) for $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$, every $\tau\in\operatorname{Aut}_L(K)$ satisfying [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.IsLevelAutAt`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelLevelAutAt.html#L29) at $\gamma^{-1}$ — the predicate saying that $\tau$ realises, on elements of $K$ given by ratios of integral $q$-expansions of modular forms of level $\Gamma_H((q\ell)^2M')$, the slash action of the matrix `conjElemN (q*ℓ) γ⁻¹`, read through a complex embedding sending $\xi$ to $\exp(2\pi i/(q\ell))$ — maps $C$ into $C$; (iii) if in addition $\gamma\in\Gamma(\ell)$, such a $\tau$ is the identity on $C$ modulo $y'$; (iv) for $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ and $\tau$ as above acting trivially modulo $y'$, there are a ring automorphism $\theta$ of $S$, an element $c\in W_0$ and a matrix $M\in M_2(W_0)$ with $\theta$ intertwining $e$ composed with the completed germ map with the action of $\tau$ on $C$, with $\theta$ fixing constants, with $\theta(X_j)\equiv\sum_i M_{ij}X_i$ modulo the square of the ideal generated by the images of $X_0,X_1$, with $c^{q+1}\equiv 1$ and $M_{ij}\equiv c\,\gamma_{ij}$ modulo $\mathfrak m_{W_0}$, with $c\equiv 1$ if $\gamma\in\Gamma(\ell)$, and with $c\not\equiv 1$ if $\gamma\in\Gamma(q)$ and $\tau\neq\mathrm{id}$; (v) two primes $P_1,P_2$ of $S$ not containing both images of $X_0,X_1$, both containing the constant $\sigma\varpi$ and containing respectively $a_iX_0+b_iX_1$ plus a term in $(X_0,X_1)^2$, have distinct contractions to the stalk as soon as $q\nmid a_1b_2-a_2b_1$; (vi) for such a prime $P$ with tangent data $(1,0)$, the germ of $a\in C$ lies in the contraction of $P$ if and only if every Laurent coefficient of $a$ lies in $\mathfrak m_A$; (vii) [`ModularCurve.jqNModC L (q*ℓ)`](def/ModularCurve_JqCoeff.html#L18) lies in $K$ and in $C$, and after subtraction of a suitable $a_0\in A$ so as to lie in $y'$, its image in $S$ is the class of some $h\in(X_0,X_1)^{e_0}$ with $e_0\ge 1$ whose degree-$e_0$ form is nondegenerate in the sense that for $a,b\in W_0$ not both in $\mathfrak m_{W_0}$ with $a^qb-ab^q\in\mathfrak m_{W_0}$ the sum $\sum_{i\le e_0}\operatorname{coeff}_{(i,e_0-i)}(h)\,a^ib^{e_0-i}$ is a unit.
--
--   **The fixed chart at $y$.** Fixed data: a point $z$ of $\mathfrak X$ with $\varpi_z$, `hϖz`, `hz`, a point $y'$ of $\operatorname{Spec} C$ with `ιFin`$(y')=z$ (`hy'`), satisfying the supersingularity condition `hss'`, and with $y'$ the ideal $y$ (`hy'y`); and a complete discrete valuation domain $W_1$, a homomorphism $\sigma_1:A\to W_1$ with $\mathfrak m_{W_1}=(\sigma_1\varpi)$ (`hσ₁`), power series $f_1,u_1,v_1$ with $u_1,v_1$ units (`hu₁`, `hv₁`) and $f_1$ congruent to the Drinfeld form modulo $(X_0,X_1)^{q+2}$ (`hf₁`), and an isomorphism $e_1$ from the completed stalk at $z$ onto $S:=W_1[[X_0,X_1]]/(\sigma_1(\varpi_t^{\,q+1})v_1-f_1u_1)$; the hypothesis `hW₁` asserts for this witness exactly the seven clauses (i)–(vii) listed above, with $W_1,\sigma_1,f_1,u_1,v_1,e_1$ in place of $W_0,\sigma,f,u,v,e$.
--
--   **Centre, blow-up algebra, valuation subring and their hypotheses.** $J$ is an ideal of $C$ which (`hJ`) equals the infimum of the set of ideals of the form $\tau^{-1}\bigl(\text{contraction along } e_1\circ(\text{completion})\circ(\text{germ at }z)\text{ of the ideal generated by the classes of }\sigma_1\varpi_t,\,X_0,\,X_1\bigr)$, the infimum being taken over $\gamma\in\Gamma(q)\cap\Gamma_0(M')$ and all $\tau\in\operatorname{Aut}_L(K)$ satisfying `IsLevelAutAt` at $\gamma^{-1}$ and mapping $C$ into $C$. $B$ is the $A$-subalgebra of $K$ which (`hB`) equals the algebra generated over $C$ by $\{x\in K: x\cdot\varpi_t\in J\}$, i.e. $B=C[J/\varpi_t]$. `W` is a valuation subring of $K$ containing $B$ (`hBW`). Further hypotheses: `hR1` (two clauses): $C\subseteq B$, and every $f\in K$ is a ratio of two elements of $B$ with nonzero denominator. `hR2` (three clauses): $A\to B$ is formally smooth and of finite presentation, and $B/(\varpi)$ has Krull dimension at most $1$. `hR3` (five clauses): an element of $L$ lies in `W` exactly when it comes from $A$; $\mathfrak m_{\mathtt W}$ is generated by the image of $\varpi$; `W` is a discrete valuation ring; $y$ is the contraction of $\mathfrak m_{\mathtt W}$ to $C$; and $f\in K$ lies in `W` exactly when $f=g/h$ with $g,h\in B$ and $h\notin\mathfrak m_{\mathtt W}$. `hEQ` (five clauses): first, for every $\mathbb F_{q^2}$-algebra structure on $\operatorname{ResidueField} A$ there is a surjective ring homomorphism $\rho$ from $B$ onto [`DrinfeldCurve.CoordRing q (ResidueField A)`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L21) whose kernel is the set of elements of $B$ lying in $\mathfrak m_{\mathtt W}$, which is compatible with $A\to\operatorname{ResidueField} A$ and which is equivariant for the level automorphisms at $\gamma^{-1}$, $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$, preserving `W`: for each such $\tau$ there is $c\in\mathbb F_{q^2}^\times$ with $(\mathrm{redQ}\,\gamma,c)$ in the subgroup [`DrinfeldCurve.hSubgroup q`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L276) such that $\rho\circ\tau=\mathtt{hAction}(\gamma,c)\circ\rho$ on $B$, and $c\neq 1$ when $\gamma\in\Gamma(q)$ and $\tau\neq\mathrm{id}$; second, $B$ is stable under all these level automorphisms; third, every prime $Q$ of $B$ containing $\varpi$ receives, under some level automorphism with $\gamma\in\Gamma(q)\cap\Gamma_0(M')$, all elements of $B$ lying in $\mathfrak m_{\mathtt W}$; fourth, an element of $B$ all of whose images under such automorphisms lie in $\mathfrak m_{\mathtt W}$ is divisible by $\varpi$; fifth, a level automorphism with $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ preserving $y$ on $C$ preserves `W`.
--
--   **Conclusion.** For $a\in C$ write $B_a$ for the $A$-subalgebra of $K$ generated over $C$ by $\{x\in K: x\cdot a\in J\}$ (the image of $J$ in $K$ being understood), and call a subring $O\subseteq K$ an *end* if there are $a\in J$ with nonzero image in $K$ and a maximal ideal $P$ of $B_a$ such that $O=\{g/h: g,h\in B_a,\ h\notin P\}$, no element of $y$ becomes a unit in $O$, and $B$ is not contained in $O$. Given a prime $\mathfrak p$ of $C$, say that a prime $\mathfrak q$ of a subring $O$ *realises* $\mathfrak p$ if $\varpi$ lies in $\mathfrak q$ whenever it lies in $O$, some $b\in y$ has its image (when it lies in $O$) outside $\mathfrak q$, and for every $c\in C$ whose image lies in $O$ one has $c\in\mathfrak p$ if and only if that image lies in $\mathfrak q$. The conclusion is the conjunction of five statements.
--
--   1.
--
--   (Trichotomy.) For every $a\in C$ with $a\in J$ and nonzero image in $K$, and every prime $Q$ of $B_a$ containing the image of $\varpi$ and contracting into $y$ (every $c\in C$ whose image in $B_a$ lies in $Q$ lies in $y$): either $Q$ is maximal; or every $f\in B$ is of the form $g/h$ with $g,h\in B_a$ and $h\notin Q$; or there is $b\in y$ whose image, whenever it lies in $B_a$, is not in $Q$.
--
--   2.
--
--   (Each end determines a prime strictly below $y$.) For every end $O$ there is an ideal $\mathfrak p$ of $C$ which is prime, contains the image of $\varpi$, is contained in $y$ and differs from $y$, and which is realised by some prime $\mathfrak q$ of $O$.
--
--   3.
--
--   (The prime is unique.) For every end $O$ and all primes $\mathfrak p,\mathfrak p'$ of $C$ containing the image of $\varpi$, contained in and different from $y$: if each of them is realised by some prime of $O$, then $\mathfrak p=\mathfrak p'$.
--
--   4.
--
--   (Every such prime comes from an end.) For every prime $\mathfrak p$ of $C$ containing the image of $\varpi$, contained in and different from $y$, there is an end $O$ together with a prime of $O$ realising $\mathfrak p$.
--
--   5.
--
--   (The end is unique.) For all ends $O,O'$ and every prime $\mathfrak p$ of $C$ containing the image of $\varpi$, contained in and different from $y$: if $\mathfrak p$ is realised by a prime of $O$ and by a prime of $O'$, then $O=O'$.
--
--   This is the local analysis, at a supersingular closed point $y$ of the $j$-chart of the integral model of $X_H$ of level $(q\ell)^2M'$ over a henselian discrete valuation ring with algebraically closed residue field, of the blow-up with centre the $\Gamma(q)\cap\Gamma_0(M')$-stable ideal $J$: primes of the blow-up charts above $\varpi$ that contract into $y$ are closed points, or points through which the whole blow-up algebra localises, or points missing $y$, and the ends of the blow-up correspond bijectively to the primes of the chart algebra lying strictly below $y$ and above $\varpi$ — one end per branch. It feeds the subsequent treatment of the ends as a valuative cover, the count of ends and the separation of Igusa branches in the Drinfeld–Igusa description of the supersingular fibre.
